# Ireena in the castle chapel (Story Allies Presence Plan, package I5; voice docs/voice/ireena.md). While Strahd holds her
# (ireena_held_by_strahd, set by strahd/ireena:taken) she stands at the chapel altar, entranced, the wedding being made
# ready (candles and stillness: her figure is her usual sprite, so nothing here says what she is wearing). The ways that
# stop him at her window wake her here too (the Holy Symbol, a cleric's or paladin's faith, a warding prayer, "remember
# who you are") and so does the Sunsword's light. Woken, she is the castle's half of the window scene:
# ireena_held_by_strahd = false and she joins the party again. Two missteps (a failed prayer or plea, each a step toward
# the altar) and the trance holds for now: the visit ends, nobody is hurt, and the party may come back. A failed
# Persuasion stays spent (docs/contracts/dialogue.md), so the Symbol, faith, the sword and a warding prayer are the ways
# on, and "Leave her" is always there. Strahd is not in this scene. While the reading has him waiting in this chapel the
# entry is hidden (data/locations/castle_ravenloft_chapel.json) and the parley says she is upstairs.
# Drafted by Gemini through the ai-bridge, edited for length and canon (docs/plans/gemini_allies/I5/).

~ start
set ireena_chapel_pull = 0
if flag.ireena_chapel_seen
-> return_sight
endif
-> first_sight

~ first_sight
set ireena_chapel_seen
Narrator: Candles burn all around the altar, freshly lit, though nobody here is tending them and the saint in the corner has no face.
Narrator: Ireena stands before the stone in her dark coat, hands folded at her waist, still as wax.
Ireena: Keep your voices down, if you would. The candles are nearly ready, and the house hates a noise.
Ireena [sad]: I thought it would be harder to stand still. Once you stop fighting the cold, there is very little left to do.
-> menu

~ return_sight
Narrator: The candles have burned lower since you were last here, and Ireena has not moved her folded hands an inch.
Ireena [sad]: You came back, and you brought the draft with you. Hush now, before you put the candles out.
-> menu

# The window's menu (strahd/ireena:window_menu), with the sword.
~ menu
* [if item:holy_symbol_of_ravenkind] Raise the Holy Symbol of Ravenkind. -> symbol
* [Cleric] Stand before her and call on your god. -> faith
* [Paladin] Stand before her and call on your oath. -> faith
* [if item:sunsword] Draw the Sunsword. -> sunlight
* [Religion DC 15] Speak a warding prayer over the altar step. -> ward | ward_failed
* [Persuasion DC 15] Ireena. Remember who you are. -> woke | woke_failed
* Leave her. -> leave

~ symbol
Narrator: You raise the Holy Symbol of Ravenkind, and the sun in it wakes against the chapel dark.
Narrator: Every candle flame leans back from Ireena as if a clean wind had come through the black window.
approve liriel_dawnsong +2 godrick_pendlebrook +1: You raised the Holy Symbol of Ravenkind over Ireena at the altar
-> woken

~ faith
Narrator: You step between Ireena and the altar and hold your faith up against the cold.
Narrator: It makes a small, honest light on the dust, and the tallow smoke curls back from her hem.
approve liriel_dawnsong +1 godrick_pendlebrook +1: You stood before Ireena at the altar with nothing but your faith
-> woken

~ sunlight
Narrator: The Sunsword blazes in your hand, and the chapel loses every shadow at once.
Narrator: Beside the altar, the newly lit candles go pale and foolish in the glare.
approve godrick_pendlebrook +1 liriel_dawnsong +1: You drew the Sunsword over Ireena at the altar
-> woken

~ ward
Narrator: You speak the old warding words over the altar step, plain and steady against the stone.
Narrator: The damp goes out of the air, and every leaning flame stands straight at once.
-> woken

~ ward_failed
set ireena_chapel_pull += 1
time +10
Narrator: The words slip away before the last one lands, and the cold settles back in. Ireena takes a small, obedient step toward the altar.
-> pulled

~ woke
Ireena [sad]: I know my name. Kolyan Indirovich found me on the road and gave me a good one.
Narrator: Her hands come unfolded at her waist, and the glassy quiet leaves her face.
Ireena [angry]: He did not raise me to stand in the dark and wait to be given away.
-> woken

~ woke_failed
set ireena_chapel_pull += 1
time +10
Narrator: She hears you from very far off, like rain against a shut window. Without looking back, she takes a step toward the stone.
-> pulled

~ pulled
if flag.ireena_chapel_pull >= 2
-> trance_holds
endif
-> menu

# Two missteps: the trance holds for now. Time is lost and the visit ends; nothing is taken from the party.
~ trance_holds
set ireena_chapel_pull = 0
time +30
Narrator: The altar candles flare tall and yellow, and the smell of hot tallow fills your throat. When your eyes clear, they have burned down a hand.
Narrator: Somewhere high in the castle a heavy door settles shut in its frame, and Ireena turns her back to you.
Ireena: You must excuse me now. Our visitor likes the room quiet before the words are said.
-> END

~ leave
Narrator: You step back over the broken pews, and she does not turn her head to watch you go.
Ireena: Do not go far. There will be plenty of room in the pews when he is ready.
-> END

# However she was woken: the castle's half of the window scene (the taking, strahd/ireena:taken, set the other half).
~ woken
set ireena_held_by_strahd = false
join ireena
Narrator: Ireena sways once and catches the edge of the dusty altar, as if the floor had been moved while she wasn't looking.
Ireena [afraid]: How long have I been standing here? Tell me plainly.
Ireena [angry]: It was the lake from my dream, cold water up to my chin, and I stood here and let it.
Ireena [angry]: Folded hands and a quiet voice, like a candlestick set out for company. I'd rather be dead in a ditch.
Ireena: And don't gawk. He took me out of my own window without my sword, and I want it on the record that I noticed.
if guest:ismark
Ismark [sad]: Look at you, standing in the candles like a saint in a window. You took ten years off me.
Ireena [smile]: Say one more word about it, brother, and I'll go down the mountain on my own.
endif
approve godrick_pendlebrook +4 liriel_dawnsong +3 thistle +2 wren_featherfoot +2 kip_smudgewick +1 ratatoille +1: You woke Ireena in Strahd's chapel and brought her out of the castle's hands
-> END
